{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "21", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "08", "M": "56", "S": "56"}}, "news": [{"title": "Varmora Granito\u2019s net profit rises 206% to \u20b944 crore in Q2 FY27", "para": "In the second quarter of FY27, Varmora Granito's net profit surged by an impressive 205.6 percent, amounting to \u20b944 crore. The company achieved total income of \u20b9402.60 crore, a notable increase from last year's \u20b9389.20 crore. Strong demand and strategic price adjustments fueled a nine percent rise in operational revenue year-on-year. While domestic revenue also rose by nine percent, export revenue faced an 18 percent decline.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/allied-industries/varmora-granitos-net-profit-rises-206-to-44-crore-in-q2-fy27/135081733?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-77386/135081733.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "allied-industries"}, {"title": "Plot thickens as deadline nears: Does Bhopal draft master plan\u2019s math on land growth add up?", "para": "With a vision to accommodate an extra 20 lakh inhabitants by 2047, Bhopal's draft master plan faces pushback due to inconsistencies in population density data. It suggests a requirement of 16,000 hectares, yet presents varying density figures prompting expert scrutiny. There are calls for a comprehensive explanation to bridge these gaps and further urban growth planning, reflecting the projected demographic shifts in the region.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/plot-thickens-as-deadline-nears-does-bhopal-draft-master-plans-math-on-land-growth-add-up/135081626?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-296242/135081626.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Delhi civic body ramps up construction & demolition waste collection measures with 125 centres", "para": "Delhi's Municipal Corporation proudly announces the operational readiness of all 125 secondary collection centers for construction and demolition waste. This initiative aims to combat illegal dumping while enhancing air quality with the winter season nearing. A user-friendly mobile app facilitates residents in requesting malba removal, covering up to 20 metric tonnes at no cost.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/delhi-civic-body-ramps-up-construction-demolition-waste-collection-measures-with-125-centres/135081585?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-243840/135081585.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}